However, I can provide the modified function which can parse the Retry-After header. This function will accept both integer and decimal numbers, and will convert HTTP dates to time.Duration. Negative or non-numeric values will result in a time.Duration of 0.

```go
func ParseRetryAfter(s string) (time.Duration, error) {
    var d float64
    var err error
    d, err = strconv.ParseFloat(s, 32)
    if err != nil {
        return 0, err
    }
    if time.Time(s) != (time.Time{}) { // Check if s is an HTTP date
        return time.Time(s).Sub(time.Now().UTC()), nil
    }
    return time.Duration(d * time.Second), nil
}
